      "content": "That makes sense. I'm currently looking at a specific dataset from the trench, and I'm seeing some really weird spikes in the salinity readings that don't seem to correlate with any measurable temperature changes. It looks like the sensor might be malfunctioning or just providing erratic values. How should I go about distinguishing between a genuine localized salinity anomaly and potential sensor noise or error?",
